      { lines: ['Production processes burn through an island, and energy is no longer cheap.', 'The climate changes, and crops can no longer grow as abundantly as they once did.', 'Frontiers are so important in these processes because they offer places where the new cheap things can be seized — and the cheap work of humans and other natures can be forcefully taken.'], flow: ['생산이 섬을 소진 → 에너지 비싸짐', '기후 변화 → 작물 감소', '그래서 새 값싼 것을 빼앗을 미개척 영역이 중요'] },
      { lines: ['Some people are more likely to cheat and steal after purchasing "eco-friendly" products, probably because they feel licensed to do so since they morally account the "eco-friendly" choice as a "good" deed.', 'Moral licensing has also been observed in the context of cooperation for the good of the environment.', 'When people are reminded of deeds they have done that they know were harmful to the environment, they might be left with a feeling of "eco-guilt."', 'People who experience eco-guilt seek pro-environmental actions to compensate for this guilt and restore balance.'], flow: ['친환경 구매 후 \'착한 일 했으니\' 속이고 훔치기도 함', '도덕적 허가는 환경 협력에서도 관찰됨', '환경에 해로운 행동을 떠올리면 환경 죄책감', '죄책감을 보상하려 친환경 행동 추구'] },
      { lines: ['In their search for such a balance, people are inclined to believe in "quick-fixes," because they want to re-establish the moral balance and escape the guilt as quickly and easily as possible.', 'In the same way that people may change their attitudes to reduce inconsistencies between attitudes and behavior, people may also change their evaluation of past environmentally burdening behaviors and future environmentally friendly behaviors.', 'For instance, people are more likely to sign a petition addressing environmental damage after viewing evidence of human-caused environmental damage.'], flow: ['빨리 벗어나려 임시방편을 믿으려 함', '태도처럼 행동에 대한 평가도 바꿈', '예: 환경 피해 증거를 보면 청원 서명↑'] }
